<title>USA: Marathon ups U.S. posted crudes 25 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>Marathon ups U.S. posted crudes 25 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 25 cents, effective Wednesday.</p>
<p>The rise brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.25 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $17.90.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana Sweet crude and Oklahoma Sweet is now $18.25.</p>
<p>((-- New York Energy Desk, 212-859-1620))</p>
</text>
